{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>I will appease his face.</b> I will nullify his wrath; and likewise ״וְכֻפַּר בְּרִיתְכֶם אֶת מָוֶת״ (Isaiah 28), ״לֹא תוּכְלִי כַּפְּרָהּ״ (ibid. 47). And it appears to me that every כַּפָּרָה that is applied to sin and transgression and to faces — all are a term of wiping away and removing, and it is an Aramaic expression. And there are many in the Talmud: וְכַפֵּר יְדֵיהּ — he needs to wipe that man's hands. And also in the language of Scripture the sprinkling-bowls of the sacred service are called כְּפוֹרֵי זָהָב (Ezra 1) — because the priest wipes his hands on them at the rim of the bowl."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:48.379122531Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}